<div class="content-block">
  <div class="section-head">Meeting Summary</div>
  <div class="summary-intro">
    <ul class="summary-bullets">
      <li><strong>Superintendent Search:</strong> The board identified a preferred candidate and voted unanimously to authorize the chair to enter negotiations; the candidate's name was not disclosed while talks are pending.</li>
      <li><strong>Top Scholars Recognition:</strong> Eighteen Class of 2026 top scholars were honored in a student-led ceremony, with valedictorian Alexander Davison and salutatorian Audrey LeBleu introducing one another at the podium.</li>
      <li><strong>FY2026 Budget Outlook:</strong> Finance Director Abigail Kitchen reported a year-end range from a $10,000 surplus to a $2.09 million deficit; city council voted to offer up to $2 million in debt forgiveness.</li>
      <li><strong>MaineCare Billing:</strong> Director of Instructional Support Kat Cox outlined the district's existing billing process (OT, speech, PT) and two potential expansions, with cautions about audit risk and documentation burden.</li>
      <li><strong>Elementary Reconfiguration:</strong> A 23-member steering committee was announced to guide the Kaler Elementary closure process; a parent survey on student placement preferences was sent the same day.</li>
      <li><strong>Educational Equity Policy:</strong> The board took a first read on a new equity policy developed by the DEI director and equity committee, alongside a first read of the updated agenda policy (BEDB).</li>
      <li><strong>Bus Safety:</strong> A parent and transportation employee raised urgent concerns about chronic overcrowding on buses during spring track meets; the superintendent committed to investigate and the board requested a June status report.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

